 "intro": "By the river Arar (Saône), central Gaul, 58 BC. The Helvetii are migrating across Gaul and have spent twenty days ferrying across the river. You are Gaius Julius Caesar, governor of Gaul, in his first campaign.",
 "debrief": "In Caesar’s own account, he marched at midnight with three legions and fell on the Tigurini, the clan still on the near bank, killing many; he notes that they were the clan that had killed the consul Lucius Cassius fifty years before. He then bridged the Arar in a day, which so impressed the Helvetii that they sent the old chief Divico to negotiate. Divico refused to give hostages, and Caesar followed the Helvetii until the battle near Bibracte. The other choices are what-ifs.",
